Consider the following ObjectScript code:<br><pre>TRY {
    Set result = ..ProcessData(input)
    If result = "" Quit
    Do ..SaveResult(result)
} CATCH ex {
    Write "Error: ", ex.DisplayString()
}</pre><br>What happens if <code>result</code> equals an empty string?

Consider the following code:<br><pre>TRY {
    Set result = ##class(MyApp.Data).ProcessRecord(id)
} CATCH ex {
    Set ^ERRORS($INCREMENT(^ERRORS)) = ex.DisplayString()
    THROW ex
}</pre><br>What is the effect of the <code>THROW ex</code> statement in the CATCH block?
